  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-04-01T02:32:17.077Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "We have a Group set up where people get verified and we block off non-verified members of the same Group using the role-restricted instances.  They are not able to join via the Group menu but they are able to get around it by asking for an invite to someone already in the instance.  So an instance only open to Role A blocks Role B people out.  But Role B person just requests invite off of Role A and gets in anyway.\n\nMy understanding is that some communities are forced to make separate Groups entirely to prevent this, but I feel that invite requests from those within a role-restricted Group instance should follow those same restrictions.",
